# invocations (representative)

$ gh-user-attachments 
exit 0
--- stdout (empty) ---
--- stderr ---
Upload multiple files as native GitHub user attachments.
Usage:
  gh-user-attachments upload --repo OWNER/REPO --file PATH --file PATH [--file PATH ...]
  gh-user-attachments auth <login|logout|status>

$ gh-user-attachments upload
exit 2
--- stdout (empty) ---
--- stderr ---
gh-user-attachments: --repo must use OWNER/REPO form

$ gh-user-attachments auth
exit 0
--- stdout (empty) ---
--- stderr ---
Manage the GitHub web session used for native attachment upload.
Usage:
  gh-user-attachments auth login            Sign in via a tool-owned Chrome window (CDP) and store the session as a 0600 file
  gh-user-attachments auth status           Show whether a usable session is configured
  gh-user-attachments auth logout           Delete the stored session and tool-owned Chrome profile residue

$ gh-user-attachments auth status extra
exit 2
--- stdout (empty) ---
--- stderr ---
gh-user-attachments: unknown auth command "status extra"
Manage the GitHub web session used for native attachment upload.
Usage:
  gh-user-attachments auth login            Sign in via a tool-owned Chrome window (CDP) and store the session as a 0600 file
  gh-user-attachments auth status           Show whether a usable session is configured
  gh-user-attachments auth logout           Delete the stored session and tool-owned Chrome profile residue

